  - path: docs/work/2026-09-05-redesign-w10-plan.html
    tier: T3
    action: added
    distills: "The WU plan, written before the code — requirement, mapping, the registry members in and hand-rolled locals out, the three changes below the screen (the short field with all sixteen values inline, StatusLine's extend, the clipboard), and a test plan concrete at all three levels with no waivers. Its load-bearing section is the deviation callout: design run #9 rules Checkbox 'its own WU, not W10', and this WU builds it anyway at the author's direction, so the plan states the cost — a registry entry with no component design file behind it, which the epic's expected result asks for — and names W11 as the inheritor rather than leaving it to be discovered."
  - path: docs/use-cases/web-ui.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "UC-ONBOARD's contract. The step rename lands in all four places the doc named 'Verify' (the step is 'make a request'; the payoff is 'the last step'). Two genuinely new observable behaviours are stated because a user can see them and could not before: a copied command confirms at the value and says 'copy failed' when the browser refuses the write, where the two calls it replaces were unguarded and silent; and quitting with a proxy still set now offers to turn it off in BOTH local cases — 'foreign' included, since unset_proxy sets the OS proxy state off without reading whose address is set — refusing to quit onto a dead proxy when that fails, and opening the manual steps instead. The remote case keeps its durable opt-out; Esc, backdrop and the dismiss glyph all cancel. CORRECTED AT REVIEW: the doc's standing sentence 'the Trust step says \"install the certificate on the device you're capturing from\"' had been left describing behaviour the build dropped — the verdict was split from its instruction and only the verdict rendered. The code now renders both, and the sentence says how (a verdict and its remedy are two elements), so the doc describes what ships rather than what was intended."
t2_note: "docs/use-cases/web-ui.html carries this WU's T2 truth — see its entry above. The quit dialog's three-mode model is stated there for the first time: the doc had NO quit-dialog content before this WU, so the mode change altered no documented claim and adds one. No decision record is owed — the build-local modal shell is design run #9's warranted proposal, now built, not a new standing rule. The Checkbox deviation is deliberately NOT distilled to T2: it is a process fact about how this WU was scoped, not a user-observable contract, so it lives in the plan, in cr/v3 and in the result report where W11 will read it. One tier-crossing correction the review surfaced: ui/src-tauri/src/setup.rs's comment on ProxyStatus still documented 'foreign => only the remote-device notice', contradicting the model the TS side now ships. src-tauri is untouched by this diff, but the comment sat one file from the contract this WU redefined, so it was corrected rather than left to mislead the next reader of the classifier."
